Spar's SCIM token and external-id stores (`spar.config.postgresMigration.scimTokens` / `scimExternalIds`) can now be backed by PostgreSQL, but there is no data migration from Cassandra yet. Only `cassandra` and `postgresql` are accepted for these two keys; spar refuses to start with `migration-to-postgresql`. Switching an existing deployment from `cassandra` to `postgresql` makes all existing SCIM tokens and external-id mappings invisible: SCIM clients must be issued new tokens, and already-provisioned users must be re-linked. Switch both keys together. Do not switch back from `postgresql` to `cassandra`: tokens revoked and external-id mappings deleted while on PostgreSQL would become valid again, and those created on PostgreSQL would disappear.
